<h2>What the library is doing</h2>

<p>
    Hashing happens with one call. The hasher is registered as a
    <code>singleton</code> in <code>Program.cs</code> &#8212; it is stateless and
    thread-safe by design:
</p>

<pre><code class="lang-csharp">// Program.cs
builder.Services.AddSingleton(new Argon2idPasswordHasher());

// During registration
string stored = hasher.HashPassword(password);
// $argon2id$v=19$m=65536,t=3,p=1$&lt;salt&gt;$&lt;hash&gt;

// During login
bool ok = hasher.VerifyPassword(password, stored);

// Optional: upgrade old hashes when parameters change
if (hasher.NeedsRehash(stored))
    stored = hasher.HashPassword(password);
</code></pre>

<p>
    Every hash contains its own parameters, so you can raise the work factor
    later without breaking existing users. See
    <a href="https://github.com/systemslibrarian/argon2id-passwordhasher#readme" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the
        full README</a> for the design rationale and complete API.
</p>
